<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεισάχθεια</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σείω, ἄχθος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shaking off of burdens</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Luc.</u>
				20
			</span></i>: a name for <i>the disburdening ordinance</i> of Solon for
			the relief of debt, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.79
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				15
			</span></i>; so of Caesar, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεισαχθείᾳ τινὶ τόκων ἐκούφιζε τοὺς
					χρεωφειλέτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
